																		AUTHOR POST
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/zzuxon" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1496981); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1496981&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606273796" alt="Zzuxon" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1496981)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/zzuxon" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1496981); return false;" >Zzuxon</a></span> <span class="odate time_1523855547 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">16 Apr 2018 05:12</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3770514">
									

<p>If you're interested in my other work, <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/author-page-zzuxon">here is my author page</a></p>
<p>I think it was 2013 when I discovered the SCP Foundation, and I was immediately entranced. After years of lurking, this is my first attempt at writing for the site. I would love to hear your thoughts.</p>
<p>Big thanks to <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/croquembouche" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2893766); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2893766&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1554650430" alt="Croquembouche" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2893766)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/croquembouche" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2893766); return false;">Croquembouche</a></span> and <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/peter-dawley" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1334168); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1334168&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1554650430" alt="Peter Dawley" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1334168)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/peter-dawley" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1334168); return false;">Peter Dawley</a></span> for giving me their feedback in chat.</p>
<p>The seed of the idea was when I was thinking about Gods of nature and how I didn't find them plausible. They were often too human, too sensible and kind to be manifestations of uncontrolled nature. Then I realized that there was one god of nature I'd read about who I thought fit the bill fantastically, even though he isn't called a &quot;god of nature.&quot; That god is Yaldabaoth.</p>
<p>Now I'm a firm believer that there is no canon, and you can interpret 3503 in any manner you wish, or no manner. But, here's what the humble author feels about it&#8230;.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Possible&nbsp;Spoilers</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;collapse</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The wild god Baker encountered is, in some way, Pan. It is also, in some way, a manifestation of Yaldabaoth. How exactly this works out is up to your interpretation, dear reader.</p>
<p>SCP-3503, more broadly, is a manifestation of Yaldabaoth's hatred of Mekhane and her gift to the intelligent peoples of the universe.</p>
<p>This is why the Church of the Broken God kidnapped Baker. His experience is of theological interest to the church. He's off being dissected/experimented on right about now.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>I hope y'all enjoy.</p>

