														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3835835">
									

<p>I'm really glad you enjoyed it. You and Daisybellus's comments are really valuable to me, because one of my big worries while writing this was that I might be inadvertantly treating the issue of PTSD in a disrespectful way. I don't have any experiences with PTSD myself, so seeing it well received by people who do is very encouraging.</p>
<p>In regards to your comments on Sarkicism, I largely agree. I actually didn't add the Sarkic tag, nor did the tagging team, another normal user did. I didn't choose to include it because the article largely deals with the conflict between Yaldabaoth and Mekhane, which isn't important to Sarkicism (And also because, in my headcanon, 610 actually isn't Sarkic, it's a direct product of Yaldabaoth himself.). That said, I didn't contest someone else adding it, thinking &quot;Hey, maybe just having Yaldabaoth is enough for the Sarkic tag.&quot; And of course more tags means more potential readers, which a writer always wants, so I sort of &quot;gave into temptation.&quot; I'll probably remove it now.</p>
<p>Your idea is interesting though. It could even be as simple as &quot;Foundation archaeologist finds a jar made by Proto-Sarkics 1500 years ago that depicts a satyr-like creature, connection to SCP-3503 is speculated.&quot; I might add something like that in, and if I do, the Sarkic tag can come back as well.<br />
Fun-fact your idea reminded me of, I considered including a brief passage where The Foundation asked some of it's contacts in the Serpent's Hand to ask actual Satyrs if they knew anything about 3503. I decided not to include it to avoid over-complicating the narrative, and because I want to use a similar &quot;zinger&quot; in another article I'm going to write.</p>

