<p>I can't upvote here, but just because it really, REALLY over-explains itself. I think the manner you dealt with PTSD was reasonable, and I don't think it tries to explains mass shootings, but just describes one fictional mass shooter. I loved the idea of an anomaly that &quot;rides&quot; a non-anomalous mental condition, it is very interesting and respectful with the fact that the main condition is real and serious.</p>
<p>But seriously, this skip can be hugely trimmed. A lot of it is completely irrelevant to your article, just adding layers and layers of detail to what was already explained. It gets worse when you go to lengths in applying fantastic explanations like psionics and super-memetics just to do with more words what should be just a brief description.</p>

