<p>The downsides are massive, but it's rare for anything, even art, to acknowledge the aspect of it that feels familiar and in a sense comforting even in its horror. Even after getting far enough away from the original circumstances to have the emotional energy necessary to do so, ime there's a big struggle internally to get to the point where the anxiety and stress of contemplating facing life without that emotional armor seems less daunting than the anxiety and stress of leaving it in place.</p>

